akdown of how to derive the answer.\n        """\n        reasoning_chain = await self.generate(instruction=question_analysis_instruction, context=self.problem_text)\n\n        # Step 3: Generate candidate answers based on the reasoning chain\n        candidate_answers_instruction = f"""\n        Using the reasoning chain: {reasoning_chain}\n        Generate multiple candidate answers to the question. \n        Ensure each candidate answer is supported by the provided context documents. \n        Format the output as a list of candidate answers with brief explanations.\n        """\n        candidates = await self.generate(instruction=candidate_answers_instruction, context=self.problem_text)\n\n        # Step 4: Revise and refine the candidate answers\n        refinement_instruction = """\n        Critique and refine the candidate answers. \n        Ensure they are accurate, concise, and directly address the question. \n        Remove any ambiguities or unsupported claims.\n        """\n        refined_answers = await self.revise(instruction=refinement_instruction, context=candidates)\n\n        # Step 5: Ensemble to select the best answer\n        ensemble_instruction = """\n        Evaluate the refined candidate answers. \n        Select the most accurate, concise, and well-supported answer. \n        If multiple answers are equally valid, provide a synthesis of the best options.\n        """\n        final_answer = await self.ensemble(instruction=ensemble_instruction, contexts=refined_answers.split("\\n"))\n\n        return final_answer\n```', '<think>\n</think>\n\n</think>\n\n```python\n# --- DO NOT IMPORT HERE ---\nclass Workflow:\n    def __init__(self, config, problem) -> None:\n        # --- DO NOT MODIFY THIS SECTION ---\n        self.config = config\n        self.problem_text = problem\n        self.llm = create(config)\n        \n        self.generate = operator.Generate(self.llm, self.problem_text)\n        self.revise = operator.Revise(self.llm, self.pr